course: dictionary
lesson: 15835
title: A big undertaking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An undertaking is a big job or project that takes a lot of time, effort or courage. Read the words around it to find that meaning. «Building the new bridge was a huge undertaking that took three years.» Huge and took three years are the clues: this is not a small job, so undertaking means a big, difficult task.
explain: Undertaking can also mean a promise. «The team gave a firm undertaking that the work would be finished by Friday.» A firm promise is made by the team, and they say the work will be finished, so here undertaking means a promise to do something. Always check: what would fit in this sentence instead of the hard word?
explain: Undertakings can be long or dangerous. «Sailing across the ocean alone was a risky undertaking.» Risky tells you the task could go wrong, so it is not an easy job.
fact: An undertaking is a big or difficult job or project.
fact: «Undertaking» can also mean a formal promise to do something.
fact: «A huge undertaking» means a very big task.
fact: The word comes from the verb «undertake», which means to take on a job or task.
fact: Undertaking can also mean the work of an undertaker, who arranges funerals.
exercise: «Building the new bridge was a huge undertaking that took three years.» What does undertaking mean? | A sad song | *A big, difficult job | A small snack | A quick nap
exercise: «The team gave a firm undertaking that the work would be finished by Friday.» What does undertaking mean here? | A type of boat | A loud noise | A game played outdoors | *A promise to do something
exercise: «Yesterday, Sam ____ a long walk across the moor.» Fill the gap with the past tense of undertake. | undertakes | undertaking | undertake | *undertook
test: «Sailing round the world alone is a major undertaking.» What does major undertaking suggest? | *A big and serious task | A game for young children | A short trip to the shops | A tasty snack
test: In a formal letter, what does «give an undertaking» mean? | A plate of food | A loud shout | A kind of coat | *A promise to do something
exam: «It was a risky undertaking, but the team was ready.» What does risky undertaking mean? | A sleepy walk | A quick game | A tasty meal | *A dangerous, big task
